    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "act": "FALSIFIABILITY",
      "narration_text": "And the catch. A universal plug is also a universal door. A tool runs with whatever permissions it's given, so a write tool really can change data. A server's descriptions can be misleading, so connect only servers you trust. And for anything irreversible, keep a human confirming the call. That's why I'd start Medhavy's interface read-only.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "lane": "remotion",
        "motion": "reveal",
